1
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:15,932
<i>If everyone's life had a genre,</i>

2
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:19,352
<i>what would yours be?</i>

3
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:27,193
<i>Film noir, with its murky underworld?</i>

4
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>A thriller driven by hidden crimes?</i>

5
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>Or a romantic comedy?</i>

6
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,341
What's the order, sir?

7
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:59,225
<i>Whatever the genre,
I'm sure everyone's lives are interesting.</i>

8
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:04,104
<i>But why did mine have to be this one?</i>

9
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,981
You have amnesia.

10
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:09,443
You have a textbook case
of dissociative amnesia,

11
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:12,446
meaning you've forgotten
key autobiographical details

12
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,282
such as your name, age, or occupation.

13
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:18,952
It's the same amnesia
you often see in dramas and movies.

14
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:19,829
Exactly.

15
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,290
- Sorry?
- This…

16
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,417
It's actually possible?

17
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:29,546
How can I not remember a single thing?

18
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:31,840
It's not as common
as you see in dramas, but--

19
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,510
And what normally happens in dramas?

20
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:38,263
Well, they usually wake up,
turn to the person beside them,

21
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:40,599
and ask with a vacant, innocent look,

22
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,975
"Who are you?"

23
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,103
Something like that.

24
00:01:43,686 --> 00:01:44,728
And where are they?

25
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:48,607
The person I'm supposed to ask
"Who are you?" with an innocent look?

26
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:51,360
Unfortunately, there is no one.

27
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:52,403
No one?

28
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:56,990
You were unconscious
when you were brought in two weeks ago.

29
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:59,493
You were found alone,
collapsed on the ground,

30
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:01,495
and your body displayed
multiple signs of injury.

31
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:04,707
And we couldn't use your fingerprints
to identify you, so…

32
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,004
What the heck?

33
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:13,966
When you were found,
your fingerprints were damaged.

34
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,885
Without fingerprints,
we were unable to identify you,

35
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,929
so we had no way
of contacting your family.

36
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:22,391
Then shouldn't there have been
an investigation?

37
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:24,935
The police tried to investigate
what happened,

38
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:28,105
but you were found on a remote road
with no CCTV cameras.

39
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:30,315
And they didn't find
any viable fingerprints

40
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:33,944
on the clothes and shoes you were wearing
when you were found.

41
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,487
Okay, hold up.

42
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:36,781
So, in a nutshell,

43
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:41,035
I was found on the road and brought here
two weeks ago.

44
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:45,038
You couldn't identify me.
The accident investigation was a bust.

45
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,166
And I lost my memory?

46
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,084
That's a perfect summary.

47
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:50,544
Then what should I do now?

48
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:52,671
It would be great
if your memory returned--

49
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:54,339
What if it doesn't?

50
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,382
If it doesn't?

51
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,593
You'll be classified as
an unidentified person,

52
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,428
and once you've been treated,

53
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:01,848
you'll be sent to a government facility.

54
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:07,854
So, put simply,

55
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:10,856
I'm in a damn sticky mess.

56
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,234
You really are excellent at summarizing.

57
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:15,862
That's a good sign.

58
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:28,290
OUR STICKY LOVE

59
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:30,209
Who are you?

60
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:33,338
How did you end up here
after such a terrible accident?

61
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:39,052
How is it possible that you don't even
remember your own name?

62
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,016
But…

63
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:47,769
you're pretty.

64
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,149
Check out this body.

65
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:56,485
Abs? Why do you have abs?

66
00:03:56,486 --> 00:04:00,072
I must say, at first glance,
I really like what I see.

67
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:03,325
With these looks,
you should have become a celebrity.

68
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:04,910
Why didn't you?

69
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:09,540
If you had, even if you had amnesia,
other people would have recognized you.

70
00:04:12,168 --> 00:04:14,128
Who the heck were you?

71
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:18,423
Damn it, who the heck was I?

72
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:20,927
Oh, come on!

73
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:28,267
SANDEUL HOSPITAL

74
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:30,103
ONE WEEK LATER

75
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:33,898
Nowadays,

76
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:38,485
government-run facilities aren't half bad.

77
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:39,403
That's right.

78
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,780
I hear they even educate
North Korean refugees

79
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:43,824
and help them find jobs.

80
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,868
Think of it as an opportunity
to start life anew.

81
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:49,788
Go there and try to find
what you're good at.

82
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:51,123
You scared me.

83
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,333
Okay, let's try whatever.

84
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:56,753
I lost my memory due to a head injury,
so if I stimulate it again,

85
00:04:56,754 --> 00:04:58,213
maybe it will come back.

86
00:04:58,214 --> 00:04:59,424
That's it. Attagirl.

87
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,176
She's got her pep back.

88
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:04,137
Fancy some peanuts?

89
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,476
Good heavens!

90
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:13,020
- Oh no!
- Goodness, dear.

91
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:13,855
Oh my.

92
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:18,734
Looks like she's coming to.

93
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:21,361
You should dial down the crazy.

94
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:24,699
Why would you smash your noggin
into the wall like that?

95
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:27,659
Or you should've waited an hour to do it.

96
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,577
Sorry?

97
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,329
Shortly after you passed out,

98
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,999
someone came by.

99
00:05:33,499 --> 00:05:35,084
Your boyfriend.

100
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:38,670
Someone who actually knows you

101
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:40,757
finally came for you!

102
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:42,257
Really?

103
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:45,887
Apparently, your boyfriend's been
looking for you like crazy.

104
00:05:46,929 --> 00:05:48,430
He has?

105
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,639
And where is he?

106
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,393
- My so-called boyfriend?
- Hold your horses. He'll be here soon.

107
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:58,691
Your boyfriend's a strapping young man.
A total looker.

108
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:01,319
I thought he was an actor.

109
00:06:03,696 --> 00:06:05,406
Aren't you lucky?

110
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,199
He was totally my type.

111
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,409
Thank God.

112
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:11,704
Of course.

113
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,083
Looking this good,
there's no way I'm single.

114
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:19,212
I can finally find out who I am.

115
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:23,257
You've been through so much, dear.

116
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,680
I hear someone coming.

117
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:40,316
<i>Oh my…</i>

118
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,322
<i>I hit the jackpot.</i>

119
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:50,034
Grandma.

120
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:52,912
There you are.

121
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:55,915
This is my grandson.

122
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,334
He's a model.

123
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,337
- Say hello.
- Nice to meet you.

124
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:05,508
I hear someone else coming.

125
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:26,863
You heard, didn't you?
That someone came for you.

126
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:29,907
Shall we call him in?

127
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,536
Come on in.

128
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:43,212
HONG'S BOXING GYM

129
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,514
<i>Who the heck</i>

130
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:57,143
<i>is this scruffy, scrappy boxer?</i>

131
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,778
<i>Why is Scrappy standing in front of me?</i>

132
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:10,740
Go Eun-sae.

133
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:16,245
You really don't remember anything?
You don't know who I am?

134
00:08:18,372 --> 00:08:20,041
<i>Yes, I'd like to keep it that way.</i>

135
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:24,462
It's me.

136
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,422
<i>No.</i>

137
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:28,381
Jang Tae-ha.

138
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:29,383
<i>No.</i>

139
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,594
<i>Please.</i>

140
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:33,387
Your boyfriend.

141
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:40,728
Moving, isn't it?

142
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:44,607
For three whole weeks,
he says he searched every hospital

143
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:48,152
in Seoul, Gyeonggi,
and the entire capital area to find you.

144
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:52,323
I heard he was a looker…

145
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:54,408
That he looked like an actor…

146
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:57,619
His shoulders are as broad as a barn door.

147
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,997
- Like a young Baek Il-seob.
- Looks like Park Geun-hyeong to me.

148
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:04,001
That's exactly how Park looked
when he was young.

149
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:15,555
So, in a nutshell,

150
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:18,015
my name is Go Eun-sae.

151
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:19,433
As for age,

152
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:21,393
I'm 33 years old.

153
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:24,396
I work part-time at a taffy shop,
making taffy,

154
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:27,816
and I've been dating you,
a boxing coach, for two years,

155
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:31,153
and we live together,
even looking to get married soon?

156
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:47,210
Well, what to do?
I don't believe any of that.

157
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:50,755
For starters, how could I not have
a proper job at 33?

158
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:53,466
You were an aspiring web novel writer
who never made it.

159
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:56,804
So you started working at
my grandmother's taffy shop a month ago.

160
00:09:57,430 --> 00:10:00,683
Then do you have any proof
that we're dating?

161
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:13,028
Hey, come on.

162
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:16,615
This couldn't possibly be proof
that we're dating.

163
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:20,077
This could be two tourists passing by
who happened to be snapped together.

164
00:10:22,079 --> 00:10:22,913
Any other photos?

165
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:26,207
- This is the only one.
- See?

166
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:28,793
How is that possible
when we dated for two years?

167
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:33,174
I lost my phone while running around
looking for you these past three weeks.

168
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:36,801
- It had all our photos.
- You expect me to believe that?

169
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:38,929
It would've helped
if we had your phone,

170
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:41,890
but, as you know,
they found you with nothing.

171
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:46,312
I have no clue what happened to you
after you went out to meet a friend,

172
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:48,230
but for now,

173
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,317
I'm just glad you're alive.

174
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,198
Do you

175
00:10:57,698 --> 00:11:00,076
usually not wash up?

176
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,666
Oh, I…

177
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:13,088
Well, my car broke down on the way here,
so I had to fix it in a hurry.

178
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,589
And you don't shave?

179
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:15,633
Shave?

180
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,844
It's been a bit hectic recently.

181
00:11:22,556 --> 00:11:23,807
Fine, I get it.

182
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:27,186
Can you just reach out
to my family for me?

183
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,397
You don't have any.

184
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:31,731
I don't have any?

185
00:11:31,732 --> 00:11:33,901
You grew up in an orphanage.

186
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,282
Hold on.

187
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:43,869
So I don't have any family,

188
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:47,122
I lost my phone,
so I don't have any friends' numbers,

189
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:51,252
and I'm an aspiring web novel writer,
so I don't have any colleagues.

190
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,962
So, in other words,

191
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:56,215
you're the only one I have
in the whole world?

192
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,842
Is that right?

193
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,679
As I said,
you're excellent at summarizing.

194
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:10,603
If you're done talking, you can go home.

195
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:13,858
You can get the rest of your treatment
as an outpatient.

196
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,070
Can I talk to you for a second?

197
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:19,655
Sure, yes.

198
00:12:22,616 --> 00:12:25,286
You should go wash your face or something.

199
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:34,377
How can you just believe he's my boyfriend
and let him take me home?

200
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:36,838
We checked with the police,

201
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:40,968
and the person he's been looking for
matched your description perfectly.

202
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:44,846
He even knew about
the triangle of moles on your butt.

203
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:46,890
He got it exactly right.

204
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:48,224
Moles on my butt?

205
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:51,227
Yes, we all saw them
when we were treating you.

206
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:55,940
Just here on your right butt cheek,
you have a triangle of moles.

207
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:59,736
And the mole at the very top
is a little different in color.

208
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,404
Greenish, if you will.

209
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:03,991
He even got that right.

210
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:09,704
Quite frankly,
those sorts of details are things

211
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,457
only a boyfriend would know.

212
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:14,584
Even so, how could you let me go

213
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:16,753
with a complete stranger--

214
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:19,256
If you don't believe him,
you can refuse to go with him.

215
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:22,300
You can wait here for the police

216
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:25,304
to escort you to a government facility.

217
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:35,731
It's true. They're in a triangle,
and one's a different color.

218
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:38,399
So,

219
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,903
everything that guy said is true?

220
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,328
Okay, I'll go with him for now.

221
00:13:49,829 --> 00:13:52,998
Who knows? Maybe going back
to where I lived will jog my memory.

222
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,215
I used to wear this?

223
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,425
I really wore something so tacky?

224
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:16,062
You have to take these three times a week…

225
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,190
I mean, three times a day.

226
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:24,071
So what now?

227
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:26,448
Do we go home?

228
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:28,492
Yeah.

229
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,420
Wait.

230
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,713
Why are we going there, not Seoul?

231
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:42,798
We don't live in Seoul.

232
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,633
Don't be ridiculous.

233
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:47,468
I may not remember who I am,

234
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:50,513
but I remember
the Seoul subway map up to Line 9.

235
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:54,017
We used to live in Seoul,
but we moved to Gujin two months ago.

236
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:55,644
We… What?

237
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:57,521
Where the heck is Gujin?

238
00:14:58,230 --> 00:14:59,189
My hometown.

239
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:15,497
HONG'S BOXING GYM

240
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,928
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

241
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:41,774
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

242
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,989
The rice came out perfect!

243
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:52,242
Come on, you can do better.

244
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:54,870
- Isn't the rice good?
- Tae-ha, you're back?

245
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:56,372
Yes, ma'am.

246
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,541
Careful, now.

247
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:20,729
GUJIN-GUN TRADITIONAL RICE TAFFY

248
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,715
Hello.

249
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,217
- Hey.
- Hi!

250
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:52,428
- Must be her.
- That her?

251
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:56,849
What the…

252
00:16:57,599 --> 00:16:59,101
Who are those rough-looking women?

253
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:06,107
If I knew I'd be lucky enough
to see your face today,

254
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,402
I would've worn my glasses.

255
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:10,319
This is her, isn't it?

256
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,780
Your future missus
who came from Seoul with you?

257
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:13,949
Yes.

258
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,244
Say hello. They're from this village.

259
00:17:20,789 --> 00:17:21,873
Do you know me?

260
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,167
Why, are you famous or something?

261
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,085
- How would we know you?
- You don't?

262
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:28,129
Never seen me around?
Apparently I live here.

263
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,715
Well, that's the thing, isn't it?

264
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:34,427
You came here almost two months ago,
but it's the first time you've graced us.

265
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:36,722
So how could we have seen you?

266
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:41,392
I apologize. We've had a lot going on.

267
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:43,478
I'll tell you the details later.

268
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:44,938
- Sure.
- You do that.

269
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:47,273
You can get going now.

270
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,901
You're in my way.

271
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:56,158
I'll get going…

272
00:17:58,452 --> 00:17:59,536
so move out of my way.

273
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:09,755
Tae-ha,

274
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:11,924
what's with her?

275
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:18,054
Tae-ha.

276
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:19,306
She's…

277
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:20,849
Oh boy, Tae-ha.

278
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:28,815
Wow, what a character.

279
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,817
That one's no ordinary girl, is she?

280
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:31,734
Definitely not.

281
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:35,447
She's clearly one of those rude Gen Z kids
who left their manners behind.

282
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:39,493
She and I will never get along,
not in a million years.

283
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,466
- Hello, I'm--
- Song-wol.

284
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:58,512
I told you, right?
She doesn't remember anything.

285
00:19:01,098 --> 00:19:04,059
Do you know me? Did I really work here?

286
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:09,857
And what about him?
Is he really my boyfriend?

287
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:19,366
Please tell me everything
you know about me.

288
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:25,038
Come on, just tell me.
You don't have to worry about him.

289
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:28,500
She can't speak. She has aphasia.

290
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:33,088
Her name is Kim Song-wol,
and she's from North Korea.

291
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:37,758
She can't speak,
but she can hear and read just fine,

292
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:40,262
so communication isn't a problem.

293
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:48,562
Excuse me, ma'am.

294
00:19:49,062 --> 00:19:50,563
Ma'am, did I really--

295
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:54,026
Keep it down, old lady!
Go outside and choke on some taffy.

296
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,821
What did you just say?

297
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:00,406
My grandma has dementia.

298
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:02,158
She didn't mean to be rude--

299
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:03,117
No, not that.

300
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,535
"Old lady"?

301
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:07,747
Why would you call me an old lady?

302
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:09,707
Why would you call me old?

303
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:13,461
If you're going to be that darn loud,
you should've become a singer.

304
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,339
Goodness, you're hurting my ears.

305
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,841
Honey, take this old lady outside.

306
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,850
What a crazy bitch.

307
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:32,564
One has dementia,
and the other has aphasia.

308
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:35,858
There's really no one I can ask?

309
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:38,195
Let's go home now.
You should get some rest.

310
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:43,158
By "home," you mean the house
we used to live in, right?

311
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:00,550
This is our home.

312
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:07,599
Well…

313
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:14,273
Hold up.

314
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:16,817
Wait a minute.

315
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:19,319
Why's it barking at me?

316
00:21:20,487 --> 00:21:23,948
If I used to live here,
it should run over, wagging its tail.

317
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:27,160
Why is it barking at me
like I'm a complete stranger?

318
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:29,746
It's not our dog.

319
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:33,709
It was in there.

320
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:35,918
That's village dogs for you.

321
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,878
They wander around

322
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:40,716
and eat and sleep
if they find a doghouse they fancy.

323
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:43,385
It's been staying here the past few days.

324
00:21:45,095 --> 00:21:46,012
Are you serious?

325
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:49,308
Thankfully, it doesn't bark for long.
It stops after a few barks.

326
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,228
This is killing me.

327
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:55,897
That makes no sense.

328
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:23,425
Flowers, flowers, flowers, and flowers.
Flowers everywhere.

329
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:27,762
Has this blanket been in the family
for three generations or something?

330
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:30,724
- It was bought recently--
- No way someone paid money for this.

331
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,644
What's with this bed?

332
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:43,820
How very old-school soap opera.

333
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:50,284
Is this chicken soup?

334
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:52,621
Why is there <i>reishi</i> mushroom in lotion?

335
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:55,999
This was really expensive…

336
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,671
I'm sure of it.

337
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:03,340
I didn't live here.

338
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:05,383
Why do you think that?

339
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:09,388
Because I don't like a single thing
in this house.

340
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:11,847
You hated superficial things,

341
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:13,808
so we didn't renovate when we moved in--

342
00:23:13,809 --> 00:23:17,353
I'm the girl who cropped my hospital gown.

343
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:20,565
You're saying I hated superficial things
when I loved to get dolled up?

344
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:25,444
And how come there's none of your stuff
in the bedroom?

345
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:28,573
If we were due to get married,
we must have shared a room.

346
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:32,243
When I found out the state you were in,

347
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:34,495
I moved all of my stuff there.

348
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:37,164
For you, it'd be like
sleeping with a man you just met.

349
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:38,542
It would be strange.

350
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:42,045
- So you were being considerate?
- Yes.

351
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,718
Your name's Jang Tae-ha, right?

352
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:51,345
Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

353
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:54,223
Tell me about how we met.

354
00:23:54,224 --> 00:23:57,560
I'm finding it hard to believe
any of this, so start from the beginning.

355
00:23:57,561 --> 00:24:00,396
A blind date?
Or did you make the first move?

356
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:06,027
I need to know how and why
I ended up living with you.

357
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,954
We met in the mountains.

358
00:24:19,499 --> 00:24:21,084
What are you looking at?

359
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:01,291
You can continue on your way. I've got it.

360
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:16,889
Are you freaking kidding me?

361
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:19,558
I fell for you
just because you caught a toad?

362
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:22,228
You just wouldn't stop chasing me.

363
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:24,563
Whoa, wait. What did you say?

364
00:25:24,564 --> 00:25:26,650
<i>I</i> pursued <i>you</i>? Not the other way around?

365
00:25:27,150 --> 00:25:30,069
You said you'd kill yourself
if I didn't go out with you, so I did.

366
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:33,322
One day, you showed up with your stuff,
so we started living together.

367
00:25:33,323 --> 00:25:37,326
You insisted you couldn't live without me,
so we decided to get married.

368
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:39,371
Wait. Hold it right there.

369
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:41,622
Look, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

370
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:45,584
Just because I don't remember anything
doesn't mean you can just make things up.

371
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:48,712
I haven't believed
anything you've said so far,

372
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:50,923
and this is by far the most unbelievable.

373
00:25:50,924 --> 00:25:52,049
Should I go on?

374
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:54,844
No, thank you.
Are you trying to give me a heart attack?

375
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:59,140
Then get some rest. I'll be right back
after returning the car to the gym.

376
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:19,660
HONG'S BOXING GYM

377
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:21,662
All right, good!

378
00:26:21,663 --> 00:26:22,497
One more time.

379
00:26:24,165 --> 00:26:26,917
One-two! Again.

380
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,377
Again, one-two!

381
00:26:28,378 --> 00:26:29,212
Good!

382
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:31,131
What's wrong?

383
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:33,758
Your shirt's still half dry.

384
00:26:34,342 --> 00:26:35,176
Get up.

385
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:36,636
On your feet!

386
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:42,601
Enough for today.

387
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:44,893
Thank you, sir.

388
00:26:44,894 --> 00:26:47,062
The more you sweat during training,

389
00:26:47,063 --> 00:26:49,106
the less you bleed during a match.

390
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:51,526
I'll sweat buckets tomorrow.

391
00:26:52,402 --> 00:26:53,403
If you say so.

392
00:26:57,198 --> 00:26:58,282
There you are.

393
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,159
Yes, sir.

394
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:01,744
Hello, Coach.

395
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:02,704
Good work, Pil-seung.

396
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,665
- Sir, I'll be going now.
- Okay.

397
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:08,417
- Go on.
- Okay. Goodbye.

398
00:27:08,418 --> 00:27:10,211
- Hey, run all the way home.
- Yes, sir!

399
00:27:16,926 --> 00:27:19,136
Hey, how did it go?

400
00:27:19,137 --> 00:27:20,305
Did you bring her back okay?

401
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:25,352
She doesn't seem to believe me.

402
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:27,353
Figures.

403
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:30,356
She must be used to
living in luxury in Seoul.

404
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:33,735
Something inside her
must be resisting the countryside.

405
00:27:34,694 --> 00:27:35,528
Do you think

406
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:37,656
it'll be okay?

407
00:27:39,991 --> 00:27:42,535
We can't get caught, no matter what.

408
00:27:45,997 --> 00:27:48,375
3 WEEKS AGO

409
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:11,064
This is a reserved space,
so you can't park here. Please move.

410
00:28:12,273 --> 00:28:13,817
- You must be new here.
- Sorry?

411
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:16,777
Yes. You must frequent
the Prosecutors' Office

412
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:18,697
to notice a change in security detail.

413
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:21,366
I have, for about three years now.

414
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:24,953
I changed my car over the weekend,
so it's not registered yet.

415
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,747
- But this is my parking space.
- Sorry?

416
00:28:28,873 --> 00:28:32,210
And I'll continue to frequent this place,
so please remember my face.

417
00:28:34,921 --> 00:28:38,967
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

418
00:28:42,637 --> 00:28:46,306
And this here is our top gun,
Prosecutor Go Ji-won.

419
00:28:46,307 --> 00:28:48,350
You saw her at the inauguration, right?

420
00:28:48,351 --> 00:28:52,188
Yes. How could I forget someone
with such a unique presence?

421
00:28:54,983 --> 00:28:57,318
I have many other
exceptional qualities, Chief.

422
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:01,489
You'll see them soon in my work.

423
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:11,916
If you'll excuse me…

424
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:15,044
Mr. Mayor, this is my girlfriend.

425
00:29:16,254 --> 00:29:19,006
Hello, I'm Go Ji-won
from the Prosecutors' Office.

426
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:22,426
Yes, I've heard a lot about you.
An anti-corruption prosecutor, correct?

427
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:25,430
Anti-corruption?
You must be one of the elite.

428
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:29,976
This is Chairman Baek Sang-gil
of Mirae Eden Company.

429
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:31,686
I'm well aware.

430
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:37,650
I found your guest introduction
rather memorable.

431
00:29:42,197 --> 00:29:43,406
It's nice to meet you.

432
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:49,537
I'll leave you to it, then.

433
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:51,998
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

434
00:29:56,211 --> 00:30:00,422
<i>The mayor and Chairman Baek will leave
the venue between 10:00 and 10:10.</i>

435
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:02,382
<i>I'm only escorting the mayor to the venue.</i>

436
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:06,054
<i>The official plan is that
the mayor's driver will take him home.</i>

437
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:09,891
<i>But instead of going home,
he'll be making contact?</i>

438
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:11,976
Don't worry.

439
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:15,313
This is valuable intel
my aide boyfriend managed to get me.

440
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:17,982
I have to make this work.

441
00:31:07,615 --> 00:31:10,994
You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor

442
00:31:11,494 --> 00:31:12,954
for the Irang-dong project.

443
00:31:13,454 --> 00:31:18,084
There are a lot of eyes on this,
so it's hard to speed things up.

444
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:25,424
Before we bring the thunder,

445
00:31:25,425 --> 00:31:28,136
it'd be best for you
to take care of it swiftly.

446
00:31:29,470 --> 00:31:32,181
We wouldn't want the thunder
to be followed by a downpour,

447
00:31:33,808 --> 00:31:35,310
leaving our dear mayor's

448
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:38,980
royal robes be drenched, would we now?

449
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:27,694
<i>You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor</i>

450
00:32:27,695 --> 00:32:28,988
<i>for the Irang-dong project.</i>

451
00:32:31,658 --> 00:32:33,284
We meet again, Prosecutor.

452
00:32:44,128 --> 00:32:44,963
Looks like it.

453
00:32:46,172 --> 00:32:48,091
Though not in the most dignified place.

454
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:56,307
We only got word of your visit
at the last second,

455
00:32:57,892 --> 00:33:00,269
so we ended up showing you
an unseemly side.

456
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:04,232
Given the chance to make it up to you,
we'd treat you handsomely.

457
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:07,485
As for your watch…

458
00:33:09,612 --> 00:33:11,656
we'd replace it quite generously.

459
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:23,751
I guess you think
prosecutors in Korea are a joke.

460
00:33:25,628 --> 00:33:27,130
I'm loaded.

461
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:29,924
I don't need your dirty money to get by.

462
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:38,182
If you're waiting for your investigators,

463
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:42,520
my men have gone to greet them,
so no need to worry too much.

464
00:33:45,189 --> 00:33:47,358
So, Prosecutor,

465
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:49,902
what will you do now?

466
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:56,659
Crazy bastard.

467
00:34:22,977 --> 00:34:23,978
Seriously?

468
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:27,398
You bastards want to…

469
00:34:28,816 --> 00:34:29,650
Hey!

470
00:34:33,488 --> 00:34:34,447
What the…

471
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:07,355
You know,
I don't really watch movies anymore.

472
00:35:08,481 --> 00:35:10,524
The ending's already decided,

473
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:13,694
and wasting all that time
just to watch it unfold…

474
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:18,199
seems fucking stupid.

475
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,600
I'm saying, don't even bother.

476
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,913
Hey! Get over here, damn it!

477
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:10,793
Fuck!

478
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:43,617
<i>You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor</i>

479
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:45,118
<i>for the Irang-dong project.</i>

480
00:36:45,119 --> 00:36:46,913
<i>There are a lot of eyes on this,</i>

481
00:36:47,496 --> 00:36:49,832
<i>so it's hard to speed things up.</i>

482
00:36:52,126 --> 00:36:54,128
What should we do now?

483
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:04,889
NARITA, TOKYO
LANDED

484
00:38:03,155 --> 00:38:04,240
I got the sales report.

485
00:38:05,074 --> 00:38:06,658
Thanks to you, Director Jang,

486
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,577
the Tokyo pachinko business
is faring well.

487
00:38:09,495 --> 00:38:10,329
Not at all.

488
00:38:13,582 --> 00:38:14,458
Tae-ha.

489
00:38:15,376 --> 00:38:16,210
Yes, sir?

490
00:38:17,753 --> 00:38:18,671
You told me recently

491
00:38:19,338 --> 00:38:21,799
that you wanted
to leave this world behind.

492
00:38:31,809 --> 00:38:32,643
You may leave.

493
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:36,397
Sir?

494
00:38:41,569 --> 00:38:45,947
You're the one who turned Geukrakpa,
some back-alley gang, into Mirae Eden.

495
00:38:45,948 --> 00:38:47,742
You deserve that much.

496
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:53,122
Sir.

497
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:01,714
Just do one last job for me
before you leave.

498
00:39:03,257 --> 00:39:05,009
We need to take care of a prosecutor.

499
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:08,679
It is a prosecutor we're talking about,
so things could get messy.

500
00:39:16,228 --> 00:39:18,230
I need someone I can trust.

501
00:39:20,316 --> 00:39:23,444
Think of it as giving me a parting gift.

502
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:25,363
Tae-ha.

503
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:27,990
Can you do it for me?

504
00:39:45,591 --> 00:39:46,592
Current condition?

505
00:39:47,718 --> 00:39:48,677
Almost out.

506
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,051
What's the order, sir?

507
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:40,271
- Forget it.
- Sorry?

508
00:40:45,901 --> 00:40:48,487
Chairman Baek asked me
to take care of this myself.

509
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:51,907
Don't get your hands dirty.

510
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:54,910
I'll do it myself.

511
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:08,048
HONG DO-YEOP

512
00:41:13,095 --> 00:41:14,180
I need your help.

513
00:41:14,763 --> 00:41:16,307
I have to save someone.

514
00:41:23,731 --> 00:41:27,234
<i>I'm certain Baek Sang-gil will scrutinize
every step of the process,</i>

515
00:41:27,818 --> 00:41:30,778
<i>illegally securing traffic CCTV footage
if necessary.</i>

516
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:34,866
<i>Fortunately, there is exactly one place
on the way to the final destination</i>

517
00:41:34,867 --> 00:41:36,202
<i>that's a CCTV blind spot.</i>

518
00:42:25,292 --> 00:42:26,126
Okay.

519
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:22,349
I assume you didn't leave any crumbs.

520
00:43:23,809 --> 00:43:24,643
Yes, sir.

521
00:43:29,481 --> 00:43:30,524
Good work.

522
00:43:38,949 --> 00:43:41,619
SANDEUL HOSPITAL

523
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:45,163
<i>How could this happen?</i>

524
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:47,708
<i>She finally woke up after two weeks…</i>

525
00:43:51,920 --> 00:43:52,962
UNKNOWN, F, 20S

526
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:54,506
<i>…but she has amnesia.</i>

527
00:44:00,512 --> 00:44:02,430
Since she has no fingerprints,

528
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:06,143
she'll be listed as unidentified
and placed in a government facility.

529
00:44:07,561 --> 00:44:09,062
Wouldn't that be too risky?

530
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:10,981
She must be kept from the outside world.

531
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:16,486
In this situation,
it'd be safest to keep her by your side.

532
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:20,114
But to do that, you would need to have
a valid reason to take her home.

533
00:44:20,115 --> 00:44:22,450
If you were family, for example.

534
00:44:22,451 --> 00:44:24,161
Or someone who is to become family,

535
00:44:25,371 --> 00:44:26,789
like a fiancé.

536
00:44:37,758 --> 00:44:41,636
The doctor said it's probably
a temporary aftereffect of the accident.

537
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:45,140
Surely her memory will come back
once she recovers.

538
00:44:47,851 --> 00:44:49,228
By the way,

539
00:44:50,896 --> 00:44:52,940
have you found a stowaway boat for Japan?

540
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:55,442
Kaito is looking for local brokers.

541
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:58,069
Okay, good.

542
00:44:58,070 --> 00:45:01,781
Once her memory comes back
and the boat's ready, we'll send her off.

543
00:45:01,782 --> 00:45:03,117
Then it'll all be over.

544
00:45:03,617 --> 00:45:06,661
Until then, we have to keep her here.

545
00:45:06,662 --> 00:45:09,915
So just bite the bullet.
Pretend to be her boyfriend for a while.

546
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,211
Okay.

547
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:20,133
Hey, don't worry too much.

548
00:45:20,134 --> 00:45:21,634
We're in the middle of nowhere,

549
00:45:21,635 --> 00:45:24,637
the kind of backwater
where nothing's changed in years.

550
00:45:24,638 --> 00:45:27,307
There's no place safer than this.

551
00:45:31,895 --> 00:45:33,439
No matter how I look at it,

552
00:45:34,773 --> 00:45:35,940
it's too unfamiliar.

553
00:45:35,941 --> 00:45:39,360
Just because I lost my memory,
it doesn't mean I lost my intuition.

554
00:45:39,361 --> 00:45:44,575
How can every corner of the house,
every last spoon, feel so unfamiliar?

555
00:45:47,995 --> 00:45:49,829
Come on.

556
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:52,415
If only these were fine.

557
00:45:52,416 --> 00:45:55,419
I wouldn't be this frustrated. Seriously.

558
00:45:59,214 --> 00:46:01,508
Just what kind of accident did I get into?

559
00:46:15,147 --> 00:46:18,066
What's that? Is that…

560
00:46:41,799 --> 00:46:42,925
What are you doing?

561
00:46:58,732 --> 00:46:59,817
Did you get

562
00:47:00,692 --> 00:47:02,069
your memory back?

563
00:47:02,653 --> 00:47:03,611
Why?

564
00:47:03,612 --> 00:47:05,072
Are you scared I might

565
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:06,615
get it back?

566
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:12,496
Unfortunately, my memory hasn't come back,

567
00:47:13,080 --> 00:47:14,665
but I did see something.

568
00:47:20,671 --> 00:47:22,338
I found this in the yard.

569
00:47:22,339 --> 00:47:25,174
You said I fell for you
because you caught one for me,

570
00:47:25,175 --> 00:47:27,094
but I'm not scared of it at all.

571
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:29,679
I could even keep it as a pet.

572
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:30,973
Hey, can you…

573
00:47:38,730 --> 00:47:39,565
What's going on?

574
00:47:43,777 --> 00:47:45,820
I guess you lost your fear
with your memory.

575
00:47:45,821 --> 00:47:47,197
Don't be ridiculous.

576
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:54,203
The doctor said head injuries
can cause all sorts of aftereffects.

577
00:47:54,204 --> 00:47:56,205
You're not my boyfriend, are you?

578
00:47:56,206 --> 00:47:57,164
I am.

579
00:47:57,165 --> 00:47:58,791
Still going with that story?

580
00:47:58,792 --> 00:48:00,043
I <i>am</i> your boyfriend.

581
00:48:01,461 --> 00:48:02,671
Is that right?

582
00:48:03,338 --> 00:48:05,506
Did you say we dated for two years?

583
00:48:05,507 --> 00:48:06,424
Yeah.

584
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:08,927
And we've been living together
since we were in Seoul?

585
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:12,013
- Yeah.
- Let's say I <i>did</i> pursue you.

586
00:48:12,014 --> 00:48:14,600
You must have liked me back
if you agreed to live with me.

587
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:17,102
Yeah.

588
00:48:17,686 --> 00:48:18,937
Then you won't mind this.

589
00:48:41,418 --> 00:48:45,839
OUR STICKY LOVE

590
00:49:32,469 --> 00:49:36,431
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
